      "writtenOn": "2023-01-17T15:44:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually, `device_is_ready()` can be false only when `watchdog_reload()` is called before the watchdog device is initialized. The same check is in `watchdog_config()`. I think there is no need to check it here, but I left it because it was here previously.\n\n\u003e I\u0027m not sure what the appropriate response would be (reboot?)\n\nRebooting introduces a risk of boot loop. I think we should print an error message and continue operation.",
